				<tr>
					<td class="windowbg2" colspan="3" valign="top" height="40">
						My guild is more or less a casual player guild, although we do raid. I don&#039;t mind too terribly when people see the need to move to a different guild, although what I typically see is, we&#039;ll get a new member, they&#039;ll ask for ALL kinds of help, getting epic parts, having our tradeskillers make them stuff, getting the 1 group and small raid PoP flags. Then, AS SOON as they get what they perceive to be the most they can out of us, they bail, without so much as a thank you. Honestly, more often than not, these are people I am glad are gone, but I do resent the fact they diverted our time and energy from more important tasks.<br /><br />To those people, I say, don&#039;t apply to our guild, go do it yourself, make pickup raids, etc. We are not playing to help you get into &lt;enter uberguild name of your choice&gt;. Yes I get angry when these people join us, milk our spell bank, get our help getting geared up, then bail. As such we have modified our ruleset so that new apps cannot request guild help during their probation, and earn the help thru participation.<br /><br />On the other hand, We&#039;ve had a few people who had been longtime members, and their RL friends or friends from their grinding etc form a guild, or all become members of an uberguild, and they want to leave to go play with them. I don&#039;t resent them their choice. I often miss some of them, as I rarely ever see them after they leave :(.<br /><br />If you want to use a guild as a springboard, be honest about it. Don&#039;t lie, misrepresent, or try to use them. We&#039;ve had apps that said their ultimate goal is to be in a time flagged+ guild. If we need the class, we might accept them anyhow. But if we know they&#039;re just passing thru, we&#039;re not gonna empty the spellbank and devote guild resources to gearing them up. Sure, they can come on the flaggings and so forth, participate in riads, and get their fair share of raid drops, but I&#039;m not going to schedule a chardok, PoSky, PoFear etc raid to help get an epic for someone who&#039;s gonna bail as soon as they hit 100aa.<br /><br />I agree with Xerxes, some people lie when they app, which is dishonorable and reflects on a complete lack of morals. I&#039;m just glad I don&#039;t know those people in RL.
					</td>
